'''Kol''' is a [[Munda language]] spoken by a minority in [[Bangladesh]]. Kim (2010)<ref>{{cite web|last1=Seung|first1=Kim|last2=Kim|first2=Amy|title=The Santali cluster in Bangladesh: a sociolinguistic survey|year=2010|url=https://www.sil.org/system/files/reapdata/85/39/32/85393268857150358467007206894440229270/silesr2010_006.pdf|issue=2010–006|publisher=[[SIL International]]|series=Survey Report|access-date=24 September 2022}}</ref> considers Kol and [[Koda language|Koda]] to be Mundari cluster languages. Kol villages include Babudaing in [[Rajshahi Division]] and [[Rangpur Division]], Bangladesh, while Koda-speaking villages include Kundang and Krishnupur.

